In article <20274@uflorida.cis.ufl.EDU> dor@beach.cis.ufl.edu (Douglas R. Oosting) writes:
>if your quoted SET commands are exact, that is your problem.  you can have
>*NO* spaces in a set command (it took me the LONGEST time to figure this out)

This may be dependent upon which version of DOS you are using.  I have MSDOS
3.3 and having considered that this might be the problem, tried entering the
set commands with spaces, but NetHack still ran.  This was command line,
however, perhaps this spaceless requirement is only in config.sys?  Anyhow,
the only way to be sure that this is not the problem is to leave out the
spaces, as Doug suggests.

>set TERM=nansi-color 
>set TERMCAP=\dos\termcap  (make sure you use backslash!)
					      ^^^^^^^^^^
Actually, you must use the '/' delimiter for nethack to run correctly.  The
program was ported from UN*X, and therefore expects this character in the
pathname, as well as NO DRIVE SPECIFICATION.

	set TERMCAP=\dos\termcap		NO!
	set TERMCAP=c:\dos\termcap		NO!
	set TERMCAP=c:/dos/termcap		NO!
*****>  set TERMCAP=/dos/termcap		YES! :-) :-) <*****

